title: Contact to APT29 Mobile Watering-Hole Lookalike Domains (america250.holiday, theowo.club)
id: 1a5a42d7-37f8-44ea-b05c-c3de0ba88063
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects traffic to the two lookalike domains the APT29 (Midnight Blizzard /
    Cozy Bear) "Poisoned Source" campaign registered as adversary-in-the-middle
    reverse proxies for america250.org and the Raffles London at The OWO hotel
    site. Both hosts served the UltimateFingerprinter script and the
    platform-specific n-day exploit chains to iOS and Android visitors, so any
    request from a corporate proxy or DNS log means a device on that network was
    steered into the exploit gate. The domains were burned after Sekoia's
    disclosure; keep the rule for retrospective hunting in the 27 August to
    3 September 2026 window.
references:
    - https://www.sekoia.com/blog/poisoned-source-apt29-watering-holes-targets-mobile-devices-with-n-day-exploits
    - https://gbhackers.com/fake-us-and-uk-websites/
    - https://secquill.com/articles/sekoia-links-russia-s-apt29-to-booby-trapped-websites-that-hacked-unpatched-phones/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/05
tags:
    - attack.t1189
    - attack.t1608
    - attack.t1557
logsource:
    category: network_connection
detection:
    selection_lookalike:
        DestinationHostname|endswith:
            - '.america250.holiday'
            - '.theowo.club'
    condition: selection_lookalike
falsepositives:
    - Threat-intel research, URL scanners, sandbox detonation or analyst pivots that deliberately resolve the published lookalike domains
    - Generic name matching on a re-registered domain after the campaign infrastructure was burned - confirm the resolution date falls in the campaign window before treating a hit as compromise
level: high
